<title>CANADA: Canada's Prairies to see sun in west, rain in east.</title>
<headline>Canada's Prairies to see sun in west, rain in east.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's Prairies on Tuesday were forecast to see sun in the west and rain in the east, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>Alberta should see sunny skies with highs of 24 to 28 Celsius.</p>
<p>Saskatchewan should see mainly sunny skies with highs of 21 to 28 Celsius.</p>
<p>Manitoba should see cloudy skies and scattered showers in the east with highs of 22 to 25 Celsius.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
</text>
